{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00XI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:31b7e2af274a48d77e75f6aa5f31bf659f14aaa47c13c4a556da895434ce5b05", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThere is another way to construct morphisms of topoi.\nThis involves using cocontinuous functors between sites defined as\nfollows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2467237e51207ad2e3efb99fd7573411bf5cc4a98f71e70f0c951786fdd30b06", "unit_id": "tag:00XI:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00XI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$u$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{V_j \\to u(U)\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{u(U_i) \\to u(U)\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{V_j \\to u(U)\\}_{j \\in J}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-cocontinuous}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e540b69110e1f9dbfeb55a964f96f12cb958dfa1c76a6fdc8febe06fea88ec73", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:68bedc1ddddce39d6a938dacee18b740c169ff716cb8b4cd2a871c009098ecfc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a functor.\nThe functor <MATH_0004> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>cocontinuous<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif for every <MATH_0005>\nand every covering <MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007>\nthere exists a covering\n<MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009>\nsuch that the family of maps <MATH_0010>\nrefines the covering <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b076de2171da6b2c0ef9b5edb9799cf7e8fe92d54ee53d5de7df8421b22f48f8", "unit_id": "tag:00XJ:statement"}
