<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nLet <MATH_0026> map to the same element\nof <MATH_0027>. To finish the proof of the lemma we show that\nafter replacing <MATH_0028> by the members of a covering that <MATH_0029> are\nthe image of the same section of <MATH_0030>\nby the two maps of (<REF_0004>). We may first replace <MATH_0031>\nby the members of a covering and assume that <MATH_0032>\nand <MATH_0033>. A second such replacement guarantees\nthat <MATH_0034> and <MATH_0035> have the same image in <MATH_0036> instead of in\nthe sheafification. Hence <MATH_0037> and <MATH_0038>\nare morphisms of <MATH_0039> such that\n<MATH_0040>\nis commutative. Thus we obtain <MATH_0041>,\ni.e., a section <MATH_0042>\nwhich maps to <MATH_0043> as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a3fdaf6979825f487c2d03615391109af57083c456869a8c3672a9be5b51bd22", "unit_id": "tag:00XK:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00XI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{G} \\mapsto (u^p\\mathcal{G})^\\#$", "MATH_0006": "${}_su$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-pu-sheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-exact-cocontinuous}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4b35186f2a49259b2f2662dfcb05e7861531ac3b2c56c29c0737049923bc5b6a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fc8e5f9d2a6fcce33e5dc0f9e6f944de3486bc246ceb6504225cfab6861dc065", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites.\nLet <MATH_0003> be cocontinuous.\nThe functor\n<MATH_0004>,\n<MATH_0005>\nis a left adjoint to the functor <MATH_0006> introduced\nin Lemma <REF_0001> above. Moreover, it\nis exact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c736fa5d219b6837763c297849cb9b15ee7945e7ce1f43e10028cf57b5009199", "unit_id": "tag:00XL:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00XI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}\n((u^p\\mathcal{G})^\\#, \\mathcal{F})\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}\n(u^p\\mathcal{G}, \\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{D})}\n(\\mathcal{G}, {}_pu\\mathcal{F}) \\\\\n& = &\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})}\n(\\mathcal{G}, {}_su\\mathcal{F}).\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "MATH_0002": "$i : \\Sh(\\mathcal{D}) \\to \\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0003": "$u^p$", "MATH_0004": "$u_p$", "MATH_0005": "${}^\\# \\circ u^p \\circ i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-exact-adjoint}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-sheafification-exact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-limit-sheaf}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:be231a650ddc99edd20581a5bf1ea72cf2b332816ef0e64c6972d3c969105005", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:233d2fca66f25ac09af02c1018af4edd277af46cd163aef7dc061fc150cd0149", "source_text": "Let us prove the adjointness property as follows\n<MATH_0001>\nThus it is a left adjoint and hence right exact,\nsee Categories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe have seen that sheafification is left exact,\nsee Lemma <REF_0002>.\nMoreover, the inclusion\n<MATH_0002>\nis left exact by Lemma <REF_0003>. Finally, the functor\n<MATH_0003> is left exact because it is a right adjoint\n(namely to <MATH_0004>). Thus the functor is the composition\n<MATH_0005> of left exact functors,\nhence left exact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:61821a755f12e49bbcc07c10f614a2ac3ceb70d636ec1d2a07ce04fa5cafa7a3", "unit_id": "tag:00XL:proof"}
